<title>ESTONIA: HANSA TO ORGANISE ISSUE FOR DIRBTINIS. [CORRECTED 14:51 GMT]</title>
<headline>HANSA TO ORGANISE ISSUE FOR DIRBTINIS. [CORRECTED 14:51 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hansapank said on Tuesday it was starting preparations for a five million dollar bond issue for Lithuanian synthetic fibre company Dirbtinis Pluoshtas .</p>
<p>The six-month bonds will yield 9.5 percent (corrects from 9.2 percent), the bank's interest rate products manager, Ulo Kallas, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Kallas added the bonds will be issued around September, but the date is not fixed yet.</p>
<p>The bond issue would be the first involving a Lithuanian company for Hansapank, the largest commercial bank in Estonia.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
